                <pb facs="0573" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/677: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Southgate</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-11T17:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 12—9:30
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. General amnesty has been decreed. All political prisoners except those
                    actually engaged in acts of violence have been released.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southgate</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
